/* The values are compared with the __fcxx_three_way of <compare>, which is
 * their <=> but for floating-point values with some versions of GCC.
 * Workaround: GCC 14 to 16, all targets, from -O2 on: <=> of floating-point
 * values evaluated with other comparisons of the same values in a function,
 * as after inlining, is taken to be equivalent where they are unordered, and
 * so can the other comparisons be (see __fcxx_three_way). */
